WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.480
Raise your hand if you walked out of an interview thinking,

00:02.480 --> 00:03.760
I knew that answer.

00:03.760 --> 00:05.240
I just didn't say it.

00:05.240 --> 00:06.960
Interviews are where good candidates fail.

00:06.960 --> 00:07.880
They have the work,

00:07.880 --> 00:10.160
they just can't present it on the pressure.

00:10.160 --> 00:12.000
And it is getting harder.

00:12.000 --> 00:16.080
In jobs most exposed to AI,

00:16.080 --> 00:19.440
young workers have 19% fewer jobs than expected.

00:19.440 --> 00:22.680
The jobs that are left out ask for more skills.

00:22.680 --> 00:26.840
And 63% of job seekers have had an interview with an AI.

00:26.840 --> 00:30.120
So I am building InterviewX,

00:30.120 --> 00:32.880
an interview coach that comes to you.

00:32.880 --> 00:36.120
You add a job, InterviewX reads the job post.

00:36.960 --> 00:40.320
It makes a practice plan up to your interview day.

00:40.320 --> 00:43.000
It takes you when it is time to practice.

00:43.000 --> 00:45.680
On a train, you call it and practice out loud.

00:45.680 --> 00:48.720
At your desk, you can test only the part that is weak.

00:48.720 --> 00:51.120
It tells you what to keep and what to cut.

00:51.120 --> 00:52.320
And before the final round,

00:52.320 --> 00:54.280
an actual human coach will help you as well.

00:54.280 --> 00:56.800
Then you are able to walk into the interview ready.

00:59.400 --> 01:03.120
Voice AI can now run thousands of practice calls at once,

01:03.120 --> 01:05.840
at any hour for a small cost.

01:05.840 --> 01:07.880
AI does the reps.

01:07.880 --> 01:09.720
Humans make the judgment calls.

01:09.720 --> 01:11.160
Now who will pay for this?

01:11.160 --> 01:14.240
Universities already pay for big interview tools.

01:14.240 --> 01:18.400
Big interview sells to more than 700 of them.

01:18.400 --> 01:19.920
We start with MBA programs,

01:19.920 --> 01:21.680
and then we sell to job seekers.

01:21.680 --> 01:23.520
Other tools create your answers.

01:23.600 --> 01:26.160
We learn which answers got job offers.

01:26.160 --> 01:28.320
Each interview makes our coaches better,

01:28.320 --> 01:30.600
and nobody else has that data.

01:30.600 --> 01:33.160
Nobody should lose a career defining interview

01:33.160 --> 01:35.280
because they did not get the repetitions.

01:35.280 --> 01:38.680
InterviewX, practice the right part at the right time.

